## What I implemented

`simple_linked_list.py` — a working singly linked list per the Exercism spec:
- **`Node`** — holds a `value()` and a `next()` pointer (initially `None`)
- **`LinkedList`** — `push` inserts at the head (stack/LIFO), `pop` removes from the head (raising `EmptyListException("The list is empty.")` when empty), `head()` returns the head node (same exception when empty), `__len__`/`__iter__` traverse head→tail, and `reversed()` returns a new `LinkedList` with the traversal order flipped
- Constructor accepts an optional iterable; `LinkedList(values)` yields the input reversed (head = last element), matching the canonical behavior

